{
  "id": "oneof_volume_source",
  "type": "relationship",
  "question": "What volume source types can a Pod use, and how is this represented in the schema?",
  "resource": "io.k8s.api.core.v1.Volume",
  "scope": "Namespaced",
  "multi_hop": true,
  "ground_truth": {
    "answer": "A Volume in Kubernetes supports many source types — exactly one source field may be set per Volume instance (a ONE_OF union in the schema). The main source types are: ConfigMapVolumeSource (maps a ConfigMap into a volume), SecretVolumeSource (maps a Secret into a volume), EmptyDirVolumeSource (ephemeral scratch space), PersistentVolumeClaimVolumeSource (mounts a PVC), and HostPathVolumeSource (mounts a path from the host node). In the knowledge graph this union is represented with ONE_OF edges from Volume to each valid source type.",
    "context": [
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.Volume: represents a named volume in a Pod; exactly one source type field must be set; name field is required and must be unique within the Pod",
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.ConfigMapVolumeSource: adapts a ConfigMap into a volume; items field selects specific keys to project as files",
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.SecretVolumeSource: adapts a Secret into a volume; secretName identifies the Secret to mount",
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.EmptyDirVolumeSource: creates a temporary directory that exists for the lifetime of the Pod; sizeLimit constrains its size"
    ],
